HEALTHCARE — Project Overview & Features List

🛠️ Languages & Technologies Used

Frontend (Client-side)
HTML5: For page structure and semantic layouts.
CSS3 (Vanilla CSS): Custom styling using CSS design variables, modern healthcare color palette (Medical Blue & Teal), glassmorphism effects, and flex/grid responsive design (no heavy frameworks).
Vanilla JavaScript (ES6+): Handles dynamic UI rendering, page logic, API calls, and interactive components.
FontAwesome 6: For medical icons, buttons, and status indicators.

Backend (Server-side)
Node.js: JavaScript runtime environment for server operations.
Express.js: Backend web framework for building REST APIs.
MongoDB & Mongoose: Database for storing users, doctors, appointments, transactions, messages, and notifications. (Includes an automatic in-memory fallback mode so it runs out-of-the-box even without local MongoDB installed).
Socket.IO: Real-time engine for instant 1-on-1 telemedicine chat messaging and WebRTC call signaling.
WebRTC: Browser-to-browser peer-to-peer technology for HD Video & Audio calls.
Bcryptjs & JWT: For password encryption and secure token authentication.
OpenAI API: Powers the intelligent AI Health Assistant (with a built-in offline medical knowledge engine when API key is not present).

All Features & Functionalities

1. User Authentication & 3 User Roles
Patient Role (user): Can search doctors, subscribe to plans, book appointments, chat, join video calls, and ask AI questions.
Doctor Role (doctor): Has a dedicated portal to manage online/offline availability, view patient appointment requests, accept/complete consultations, and start calls.
Admin Role (admin): Platform control panel to view system statistics, approve/reject doctor verification applications, and activate/deactivate user accounts.
Security: Passwords encrypted with bcryptjs, JWT session tokens, show/hide password toggle, and 1-click Demo Login buttons for instant testing.

2. Landing Page
Hero Section: Modern headline "Healthcare, Whenever You Need It", platform statistics counter, and visual preview.
Healthcare Services: Interactive cards for Doctor Consultation, Instant Chat, Audio Call, Video Call, AI Assistant, and Appointment Booking.
3-Step Guide: Explains how patients register, choose a doctor, and start consultation.
Pricing Preview: Showcase of care subscription plans.

3. Doctor Marketplace & Live Search
Dynamic Search Bar: Search doctors by Name, Hospital, or Symptoms.
Multi-Filter Options: Filter by Specialization (Cardiology, Pediatrics, Dermatology, Neurology, Orthopedics, General Physician), Rating (4.5★+), Max Fee, and Location.
Doctor Cards: Displays doctor photo, name, qualification, experience, hospital, fee, ratings, and online/offline status dot.
Quick Actions: View Profile, Book Appointment, and Direct Chat.

4. Doctor Profile & Slot Selection
Detailed doctor background, qualification, bio, location, patient reviews, and consultation hours.
Interactive booking modal allowing patients to select consultation type (Video, Audio, Chat), preferred date, time slot, and reason for visit.

5. Subscription & Payment Gateway
Care Plans:
Weekly Pass (₹199 / week): Basic chat & booking.
Monthly Care (₹499 / month — Most Popular): Unlimited doctor chat, audio/video calls & priority support.
Yearly Family (₹3999 / year): Full family health access & maximum savings.
Gated Access: Regular users must have an active subscription to access doctor chat and video booking.
Payment Summary Modal: Displays base price, 18% GST calculation, total amount, payment method selector (UPI, Credit/Debit Card, NetBanking), and order ID generation.

6. Billing & Transaction History
Table listing Transaction ID, Plan, Amount Paid, GST, Payment Method, Date, and Status badges (Successful, Pending, Failed, Refunded).
Interactive Download Invoice / Receipt modal view.

7. Real-Time Telemedicine Chat
WhatsApp/Telegram-style 1-on-1 telemedicine chat layout powered by Socket.IO.
Features online/offline indicators, typing indicator ("Doctor is typing..."), message timestamps, read receipts, and direct buttons to launch video or audio calls.

8. Zoom-Style WebRTC Video & Audio Consultation
HD peer-to-peer video screen showing doctor stream with picture-in-picture local video preview.
In-Call Toolbar: Mute/Unmute microphone, Camera On/Off toggle, Screen Sharing, and End Call button.
Call Overlay: Doctor name badge, connection status, and real-time call duration timer.

9. Global Floating AI Health Assistant ("HEALTHCARE AI")
Floating circular button anchored on the bottom-right corner across all authenticated pages.
Quick Prompt Pills: One-click questions for Twisted Ankle, Mild Headache, and Minor Cut.
Safety Guardrails: Prominently displays disclaimers that AI is for educational guidance only.
Emergency Protection: Automatically detects severe keywords (chest pain, difficulty breathing, stroke, severe bleeding) and displays an urgent Red Emergency Warning card directing the user to dial 108 or 911 immediately.

10. Interactive Notification Bell Dropdown
Located in the top navigation bar with an unread badge counter.
Toggles a dropdown showing alerts for confirmed appointments, active subscription updates, and doctor messages.
Includes a "Mark all as read" button to clear notifications.

11. Doctor Portal Dashboard
Online/Offline Status Toggle: Doctors can switch status to accept or pause incoming patient bookings.
Patient Appointment Queue: Table of patient requests with instant buttons to Start HD Video Call, Open Chat, or Mark Completed.
Earnings & Metrics: Track today's appointments, total earnings (e.g. ₹12,450), total patients served, and average rating.

12. Admin Control Panel Dashboard
KPI Metrics: Total Patients, Verified Doctors, Active Subscriptions, and Total Revenue.
Visual SVG Revenue Chart: Smooth curve representing monthly subscription growth.
Doctor Verification System: Table listing doctor applications with instant Approve or Reject actions.
User Management: Activate or Deactivate patient accounts

13. Profile Settings
Allows updating full name, phone number, date of birth, gender, home address, emergency contact phone, and profile avatar image URL.
